<!--
  Plain cloud "backed up" marker with a BAKED drop shadow — the badge used on a
  REAL thumbnail (video frame / image), where the ground brightness is arbitrary
  and theme-independent. A plain white cloud washes out on a bright frame; the
  offset ~70%-black copy underneath gives it a dark edge so it reads on light OR
  dark artwork, in either theme (the same "shadow behind the glyph" trick the
  grid title text uses). Self-coloured — do NOT tint at the use site.
  The pastel FALLBACK tiles (audio/doc) use plain cloud_24 tinted
  colorOnSurfaceVariant instead; see DownloadItemAdapter.

  NO CHECK MARK, deliberately (this replaced a cloud_done glyph): the badge is
  rendered at 12-14dp, and at that size the tick inside the cloud silhouette is
  mush — it reads as a smudge on the glyph, not as a state. The mark is only
  ever shown for a positively-backed-up file, so the tick was confirming
  something the badge's mere presence already says. Don't re-add it.
-->
